al Acc 0.5565 | Val Macro-F1 0.5790 | 234.8s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.885, Low pain=0.177, Moderate pain=0.611, High pain=0.644\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5416  486   96    0]\n [ 812  150   23    0]\n [  11   51  142    0]\n [   5   26    0   28]]\n  No improvement for 2 epoch(s) (best=0.5944 @ epoch 21)\nEpoch 24/30 | FT | Train Loss 0.0342 | Val Loss 0.0677 | Val Acc 0.8130 | Val Bal Acc 0.5308 | Val Macro-F1 0.5767 | 274.0s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.898, Low pain=0.250, Moderate pain=0.712, High pain=0.447\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5516  447   35    0]\n [ 751  216   18    0]\n [  21   41  142    0]\n [   2   40    0   17]]\n  No improvement for 3 epoch(s) (best=0.5944 @ epoch 21)\nEpoch 25/30 | FT | Train Loss 0.0331 | Val Loss 0.0696 | Val Acc 0.8236 | Val Bal Acc 0.5247 | Val Macro-F1 0.5696 | 226.5s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.905, Low pain=0.240, Moderate pain=0.706, High pain=0.427\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5618  343   37    0]\n [ 774  192   19    0]\n [  26   36  142    0]\n [   2   41    0   16]]\n  No improvement for 4 epoch(s) (best=0.5944 @ epoch 21)\nEpoch 26/30 | FT | Train Loss 0.0338 | Val Loss 0.0683 | Val Acc 0.8191 | Val Bal Acc 0.5330 | Val Macro-F1 0.5909 | 219.5s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.901, Low pain=0.246, Moderate pain=0.729, High pain=0.487\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5573  407   18    0]\n [ 762  206   17    0]\n [  27   40  137    0]\n [   4   36    0   19]]\n  No improvement for 5 epoch(s) (best=0.5944 @ epoch 21)\n\n>>> Early stopping triggered at epoch 26 (no improvement in 5 epochs)\n\n=================================================================\nSTAGE 09B COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY\n=================================================================\nBest checkpoint  : /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09b/best_resnet18_stage09b.pth\nTraining history : /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09b/training_history_stage09b.csv\nSummary          : /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09b/stage09b_summary.json\nBest Val Macro-F1: 0.5944  (Stage 09 baseline was 0.4666)\nBest epoch       : 21\nTest set         : NOT USED\nStage 05B split  : UNCHANGED\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ================================================================\n# CAPSTONE — STAGE 09C | STABILIZED + ORDINAL (CORAL) MODEL\n# Fixes applied vs Stage 09B:\n#   1. No frozen-backbone phase (it was net-negative: F1 0.035->0.013)\n#   2. Lower fine-tune LR (5e-5) + ReduceLROnPlateau on val_macro_f1\n#      instead of cosine annealing (09B oscillated 0.594<->0.570 late)\n#   3. CORAL ordinal loss instead of Focal Loss — treats the 4 pain\n#      levels as an ordered scale so adjacent-class errors (the\n#      No<->Low confusion that capped 09B) are penalized less than\n#      distant ones, and the boundary gets direct gradient signal\n#   4. WeightedRandomSampler kept (still needed for the imbalance)\n#   5. Early-stop patience raised to 8 (09B's F1 oscillated within\n#      a band rather than monotonically plateauing)\n#   6. Checkpoint selection uses a 3-epoch moving average of\n#      val_macro_f1, not the raw per-epoch value, since minority\n#      classes (59 High-pain / 919 Low-pain val examples) make the\n#      raw metric noisy\n# ================================================================\nimport os, json, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader, WeightedRandomSampler\nfrom torchvision import transforms, models\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (\n    accuracy_score,\n    balanced_accuracy_score,\n    f1_score,\n    confusion_matrix,\n)\n\nBASE = Path(\"/kaggle/working/capstone\")\nDATA = BASE / \"metadata\" / \"stage07\"\nOUT = BASE / \"models\" / \"stage09c\"\nOUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"CAPSTONE — STAGE 09C\")\nprint(\"Stabilized Fine-Tuning + CORAL Ordinal Loss\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Configuration\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nSEED = 42\nIMG_SIZE = 224\nBATCH_SIZE = 32\nNUM_WORKERS = 2\nMAX_EPOCHS = 35\nLR_FINETUNE = 5e-5          # lower than 09B's 1e-4; no frozen warmup phase\nWEIGHT_DECAY = 1e-4\nNUM_CLASSES = 4\nNUM_THRESHOLDS = NUM_CLASSES - 1   # CORAL uses K-1 binary thresholds\nDROPOUT_P = 0.4\nEARLY_STOP_PATIENCE = 8            # 09B oscillated within a band; give it room\nMOVING_AVG_WINDOW = 3               # smooth val_macro_f1 for checkpoint selection\nPLATEAU_PATIENCE = 3                # ReduceLROnPlateau patience\nPLATEAU_FACTOR = 0.5\n\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nprint(f\"\\nDevice : {device}\")\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    print(f\"GPU    : {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Load manifests (Stage 07 model-ready splits — UNCHANGED)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ntrain = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"train_model.csv\")\nval = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"validation_model.csv\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nTrain      : {len(train):,}\")\nprint(f\"Validation : {len(val):,}\")\n\nlabels_map = {0: \"No pain\", 1: \"Low pain\", 2: \"Moderate pain\", 3: \"High pain\"}\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Transforms — same as 09B (this part worked fine)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ntrain_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE + 20, IMG_SIZE + 20)),\n    transforms.RandomCrop((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5),\n    transforms.RandomRotation(degrees=10),\n    transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.2, contrast=0.2, saturation=0.1),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n])\n\nval_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n])\n\n\nclass PainDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, df, transform):\n        self.df = df.reset_index(drop=True)\n        self.transform = transform\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.df)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        r = self.df.iloc[i]\n        img = Image.open(r.image_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n        img = self.transform(img)\n        y = torch.tensor(int(r.pain_class), dtype=torch.long)\n        return img, y\n\n\ntrain_ds = PainDataset(train, train_tf)\nval_ds = PainDataset(val, val_tf)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# WeightedRandomSampler — kept from 09B, still needed\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nclass_counts = train.pain_class.value_counts().sort_index()\nclass_sample_weights = {int(k): 1.0 / v for k, v in class_counts.items()}\nsample_weights = train.pain_class.map(class_sample_weights).values.astype(np.float64)\nsampler = WeightedRandomSampler(\n    weights=sample_weights, num_samples=len(sample_weights), replacement=True,\n)\n\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(\n    train_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, sampler=sampler,\n    num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True,\n)\nval_loader = DataLoader(\n    val_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False,\n    num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True,\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSampler class weights (1/frequency):\")\nfor k, v in class_sample_weights.items():\n    print(f\"  {labels_map[k]:15s}: {v:.6f}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Model — ResNet18 backbone, CORAL head\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# CORAL (Cao, Mirjalili & Raschka 2020) reframes K-class ordinal\n# classification as K-1 binary \"is rank > k\" tasks that SHARE a\n# single linear layer's weight vector but have independent biases.\n# This guarantees rank-monotonic predictions and, critically, the\n# loss for each threshold only involves the two classes either side\n# of it, so a No<->Low mistake is penalized independently of (and\n# much more directly than) a No<->High mistake — unlike softmax CE\n# where all classes compete flatly.\nclass CoralResNet(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, num_thresholds, dropout_p=0.4):\n        super().__init__()\n        backbone = models.resnet18(weights=models.ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT)\n        in_features = backbone.fc.in_features\n        backbone.fc = nn.Identity()\n        self.backbone = backbone\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(p=dropout_p)\n        # Single shared weight vector -> one logit per threshold via bias offsets\n        self.fc = nn.Linear(in_features, 1, bias=False)\n        self.thresholds = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(num_thresholds))\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        feats = self.backbone(x)\n        feats = self.dropout(feats)\n        base_logit = self.fc(feats)                     # (B, 1)\n        logits = base_logit + self.thresholds            # (B, K-1) via broadcasting\n        return logits\n\n\nmodel = CoralResNet(NUM_THRESHOLDS, dropout_p=DROPOUT_P).to(device)\n\n# All params trainable from epoch 1 — no frozen phase (09B showed\n# 3 frozen epochs actively hurt: F1 went 0.035 -> 0.024 -> 0.013)\nfor p in model.parameters():\n    p.requires_grad = True\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# CORAL loss + label encoding/decoding helpers\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ndef coral_encode(y, num_classes):\n    \"\"\"y: (B,) int labels -> (B, K-1) binary targets.\n    target[k] = 1 if true_label > k, for k in 0..K-2.\"\"\"\n    y = y.unsqueeze(1)\n    levels = torch.arange(num_classes - 1, device=y.device).unsqueeze(0)\n    return (y > levels).float()\n\n\ndef coral_loss(logits, levels):\n    \"\"\"Sum of binary cross-entropy across the K-1 thresholds.\"\"\"\n    return F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(logits, levels, reduction=\"none\").sum(1).mean()\n\n\ndef coral_predict(logits):\n    \"\"\"Convert K-1 threshold probabilities back to a class index.\n    Predicted rank = number of thresholds exceeded (prob > 0.5).\"\"\"\n    probs = torch.sigmoid(logits)\n    return (probs > 0.5).sum(1)\n\n\n# Class weights still matter for CORAL — weight each sample's loss\n# contribution by inverse frequency of its true class so minority\n# ranks aren't drowned out in the threshold-wise BCE sums either.\ncounts = train.pain_class.value_counts().sort_index()\nclass_weight_lookup = torch.tensor(\n    [len(train) / (NUM_CLASSES * counts.get(i, 0)) for i in range(NUM_CLASSES)],\n    dtype=torch.float32, device=device,\n)\nclass_weight_lookup = class_weight_lookup / class_weight_lookup.sum() * NUM_CLASSES\n\nprint(\"\\nPer-class loss weights (for CORAL sample weighting):\")\nfor i, w in enumerate(class_weight_lookup):\n    print(f\"  {labels_map[i]:15s}: {w.item():.4f}\")\n\n\ndef weighted_coral_loss(logits, y, num_classes, class_weights):\n    levels = coral_encode(y, num_classes)\n    per_sample = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(\n        logits, levels, reduction=\"none\"\n    ).sum(1)                       # (B,)\n    w = class_weights[y]           # (B,)\n    return (per_sample * w).mean()\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Optimizer / scheduler — single phase, plateau-based LR decay\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\noptimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=LR_FINETUNE, weight_decay=WEIGHT_DECAY)\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(\n    optimizer, mode=\"max\", factor=PLATEAU_FACTOR, patience=PLATEAU_PATIENCE,\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Training loop with early stopping on a smoothed val_macro_f1\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nhistory = []\nval_f1_raw_history = []\nbest_f1_smoothed = -1\nbest_epoch = -1\nepochs_without_improvement = 0\n\nfor epoch in range(1, MAX_EPOCHS + 1):\n    start = time.time()\n    model.train()\n\n    train_loss = 0\n    train_true, train_pred = [], []\n\n    for images, lbls in train_loader:\n        images = images.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n        lbls = lbls.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n        logits = model(images)\n        loss = weighted_coral_loss(logits, lbls, NUM_CLASSES, class_weight_lookup)\n        loss.backward()\n        optimizer.step()\n\n        train_loss += loss.item() * images.size(0)\n        train_true.extend(lbls.detach().cpu().numpy())\n        train_pred.extend(coral_predict(logits).detach().cpu().numpy())\n\n    train_loss /= len(train_ds)\n    train_acc = accuracy_score(train_true, train_pred)\n    train_f1 = f1_score(train_true, train_pred, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\n\n    # ---- Validation ----\n    model.eval()\n    val_loss = 0\n    val_true, val_pred = [], []\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for images, lbls in val_loader:\n            images = images.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n            lbls = lbls.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n\n            logits = model(images)\n            loss = weighted_coral_loss(logits, lbls, NUM_CLASSES, class_weight_lookup)\n\n            val_loss += loss.item() * images.size(0)\n            val_true.extend(lbls.cpu().numpy())\n            val_pred.extend(coral_predict(logits).cpu().numpy())\n\n    val_loss /= len(val_ds)\n    val_acc = accuracy_score(val_true, val_pred)\n    val_bal_acc = balanced_accuracy_score(val_true, val_pred)\n    val_f1 = f1_score(val_true, val_pred, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\n    val_f1_per_class = f1_score(\n        val_true, val_pred, average=None, zero_division=0, labels=list(range(NUM_CLASSES))\n    )\n    cm = confusion_matrix(val_true, val_pred, labels=list(range(NUM_CLASSES)))\n\n    # Smoothed metric for checkpointing/early-stop (raw F1 is noisy —\n    # only 59 High-pain / 919 Low-pain val examples in 09B's run)\n    val_f1_raw_history.append(val_f1)\n    window = val_f1_raw_history[-MOVING_AVG_WINDOW:]\n    val_f1_smoothed = float(np.mean(window))\n\n    scheduler.step(val_f1_smoothed)\n\n    elapsed = time.time() - start\n\n    row = {\n        \"epoch\": epoch,\n        \"train_loss\": train_loss,\n        \"train_accuracy\": train_acc,\n        \"train_macro_f1\": train_f1,\n        \"val_loss\": val_loss,\n        \"val_accuracy\": val_acc,\n        \"val_balanced_accuracy\": val_bal_acc,\n        \"val_macro_f1\": val_f1,\n        \"val_macro_f1_smoothed\": val_f1_smoothed,\n        \"lr\": optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"],\n        \"time_sec\": elapsed,\n    }\n    for i in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n        row[f\"val_f1_class_{i}_{labels_map[i].replace(' ', '_')}\"] = val_f1_per_class[i]\n    history.append(row)\n\n    print(\n        f\"Epoch {epoch:02d}/{MAX_EPOCHS} | \"\n        f\"Train Loss {train_loss:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Loss {val_loss:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Acc {val_acc:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Bal Acc {val_bal_acc:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Macro-F1 {val_f1:.4f} (smoothed {val_f1_smoothed:.4f}) | \"\n        f\"LR {optimizer.param_groups[0]['lr']:.2e} | \"\n        f\"{elapsed:.1f}s\"\n    )\n    print(f\"  Per-class F1: \" + \", \".join(\n        f\"{labels_map[i]}={val_f1_per_class[i]:.3f}\" for i in range(NUM_CLASSES)\n    ))\n    print(f\"  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\\n{cm}\")\n\n    # ---- Best checkpoint (on smoothed F1) + early stopping ----\n    if val_f1_smoothed > best_f1_smoothed:\n        best_f1_smoothed = val_f1_smoothed\n        best_epoch = epoch\n        epochs_without_improvement = 0\n\n        torch.save({\n            \"stage\": \"09c\",\n            \"epoch\": epoch,\n            \"model_state_dict\": model.state_dict(),\n            \"optimizer_state_dict\": optimizer.state_dict(),\n            \"best_val_macro_f1_raw\": val_f1,\n            \"best_val_macro_f1_smoothed\": best_f1_smoothed,\n            \"class_weight_lookup\": class_weight_lookup.detach().cpu(),\n            \"seed\": SEED,\n            \"img_size\": IMG_SIZE,\n            \"num_classes\": NUM_CLASSES,\n            \"confusion_matrix\": cm.tolist(),\n        }, OUT / \"best_resnet18_coral_stage09c.pth\")\n\n        print(f\"  ✓ Best checkpoint saved (smoothed Macro-F1={best_f1_smoothed:.4f}, \"\n              f\"raw={val_f1:.4f})\")\n    else:\n        epochs_without_improvement += 1\n        print(f\"  No improvement for {epochs_without_improvement} epoch(s) \"\n              f\"(best smoothed={best_f1_smoothed:.4f} @ epoch {best_epoch})\")\n\n    if epochs_without_improvement >= EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE:\n        print(f\"\\n>>> Early stopping triggered at epoch {epoch} \"\n              f\"(no improvement in {EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE} epochs)\")\n        break\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Save history + summary\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nhistory_df = pd.DataFrame(history)\nhistory_df.to_csv(OUT / \"training_history_stage09c.csv\", index=False)\n\nbest_row = history_df.loc[history_df[\"epoch\"] == best_epoch].iloc[0]\n\nsummary = {\n    \"stage\": \"09c\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"model\": \"ResNet18 backbone + CORAL ordinal head\",\n    \"pretrained\": True,\n    \"image_size\": IMG_SIZE,\n    \"batch_size\": BATCH_SIZE,\n    \"max_epochs\": MAX_EPOCHS,\n    \"epochs_run\": len(history_df),\n    \"lr_finetune\": LR_FINETUNE,\n    \"loss\": \"Weighted CORAL (ordinal binary-threshold BCE, class-weighted)\",\n    \"sampler\": \"WeightedRandomSampler (inverse class frequency)\",\n    \"scheduler\": f\"ReduceLROnPlateau(factor={PLATEAU_FACTOR}, patience={PLATEAU_PATIENCE})\",\n    \"early_stop_patience\": EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE,\n    \"checkpoint_selection_metric\": f\"{MOVING_AVG_WINDOW}-epoch moving average of val_macro_f1\",\n    \"best_epoch\": int(best_epoch),\n    \"best_validation_macro_f1_smoothed\": float(best_f1_smoothed),\n    \"best_validation_macro_f1_raw\": float(best_row.val_macro_f1),\n    \"best_validation_accuracy\": float(best_row.val_accuracy),\n    \"best_validation_balanced_accuracy\": float(best_row.val_balanced_accuracy),\n    \"test_evaluation\": False,\n    \"stage05b_split_modified\": False,\n    \"improvements_over_stage09b\": [\n        \"Removed frozen-backbone warmup (09B showed it was net-negative: \"\n        \"F1 dropped 0.035->0.013 across 3 frozen epochs)\",\n        \"Lower fine-tune LR (5e-5 vs 1e-4) to reduce late-epoch oscillation\",\n        \"ReduceLROnPlateau instead of cosine annealing, tied to val_macro_f1\",\n        \"CORAL ordinal loss instead of Focal Loss — directly targets the \"\n        \"No<->Low boundary confusion that capped 09B's Low-pain F1 at ~0.3\",\n        \"Checkpoint selection + early stopping use a 3-epoch moving average \"\n        \"of val_macro_f1 rather than the noisy raw per-epoch value\",\n        \"Early-stop patience raised 5->8 given 09B's oscillating (not \"\n        \"monotonic) F1 curve\",\n    ],\n    \"known_limitations_still_open\": [\n        \"Still frame-level, not sequence-aware — onset/offset frames \"\n        \"remain inherently ambiguous per-frame\",\n        \"Validation set has only ~59 High-pain and ~919 Low-pain examples, \"\n        \"so per-class F1 will still carry meaningful noise\",\n    ],\n}\n\nwith open(OUT / \"stage09c_summary.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"STAGE 09C COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(f\"Best checkpoint  : {OUT / 'best_resnet18_coral_stage09c.pth'}\")\nprint(f\"Training history : {OUT / 'training_history_stage