 Val Loss 0.1161 | Val Acc 0.8035 | Val Bal Acc 0.5986 | Val Macro-F1 0.4929 (smoothed 0.5163) | LR 5.00e-05 | 232.9s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.893, Low pain=0.044, Moderate pain=0.363, High pain=0.671\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5622   34  335    7]\n [ 919   23   43    0]\n [  44    3  130   27]\n [   8    0    4   47]]\n  No improvement for 2 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\nEpoch 17/35 | Train Loss 0.3158 | Val Loss 0.1247 | Val Acc 0.8010 | Val Bal Acc 0.6042 | Val Macro-F1 0.5426 (smoothed 0.5035) | LR 5.00e-05 | 233.5s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.890, Low pain=0.027, Moderate pain=0.389, High pain=0.865\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5601   54  343    0]\n [ 930   14   41    0]\n [  59    1  144    0]\n [   4    1    9   45]]\n  No improvement for 3 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\nEpoch 18/35 | Train Loss 0.3007 | Val Loss 0.1209 | Val Acc 0.8311 | Val Bal Acc 0.5671 | Val Macro-F1 0.5495 (smoothed 0.5283) | LR 2.50e-05 | 231.2s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.909, Low pain=0.027, Moderate pain=0.530, High pain=0.731\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5830   30  138    0]\n [ 930   14   41    0]\n [  58    2  144    0]\n [   8    1   16   34]]\n  No improvement for 4 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\nEpoch 19/35 | Train Loss 0.2922 | Val Loss 0.1205 | Val Acc 0.8282 | Val Bal Acc 0.5936 | Val Macro-F1 0.5667 (smoothed 0.5529) | LR 2.50e-05 | 233.6s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.907, Low pain=0.036, Moderate pain=0.515, High pain=0.808\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5797   39  162    0]\n [ 925   19   41    0]\n [  51    8  145    0]\n [   8    0   11   40]]\n  No improvement for 5 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\nEpoch 20/35 | Train Loss 0.2868 | Val Loss 0.1508 | Val Acc 0.6318 | Val Bal Acc 0.4994 | Val Macro-F1 0.4158 (smoothed 0.5106) | LR 2.50e-05 | 236.9s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.771, Low pain=0.010, Moderate pain=0.179, High pain=0.703\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[4393  376 1229    0]\n [ 939    7   39    0]\n [  56    2  146    0]\n [  10    0   17   32]]\n  No improvement for 6 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\nEpoch 21/35 | Train Loss 0.2826 | Val Loss 0.1208 | Val Acc 0.8100 | Val Bal Acc 0.6022 | Val Macro-F1 0.5438 (smoothed 0.5088) | LR 2.50e-05 | 244.1s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.897, Low pain=0.033, Moderate pain=0.446, High pain=0.800\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5659   83  255    1]\n [ 910   18   57    0]\n [  47    4  150    3]\n [  10    0    7   42]]\n  No improvement for 7 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\nEpoch 22/35 | Train Loss 0.2787 | Val Loss 0.1095 | Val Acc 0.8046 | Val Bal Acc 0.6262 | Val Macro-F1 0.5629 (smoothed 0.5075) | LR 1.25e-05 | 261.4s\n  Per-class F1: No pain=0.895, Low pain=0.143, Moderate pain=0.382, High pain=0.832\n  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\n[[5545   89  364    0]\n [ 803   83   99    0]\n [  39    5  160    0]\n [   6    1   10   42]]\n  No improvement for 8 epoch(s) (best smoothed=0.5557 @ epoch 14)\n\n>>> Early stopping triggered at epoch 22 (no improvement in 8 epochs)\n\n=================================================================\nSTAGE 09C COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY\n=================================================================\nBest checkpoint  : /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09c/best_resnet18_coral_stage09c.pth\nTraining history : /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09c/training_history_stage09c.csv\nSummary          : /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09c/stage09c_summary.json\nBest Macro-F1    : smoothed=0.5557, raw=0.5811\n  (Stage 09 baseline: 0.4666  |  Stage 09B: 0.5944)\nBest epoch       : 14\nTest set         : NOT USED\nStage 05B split  : UNCHANGED\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ================================================================\n# CAPSTONE — STAGE 09-DIAGNOSTIC\n# Visual audit: are No-pain <-> Low-pain frames actually separable?\n#\n# Both 09B (Focal Loss) and 09C (CORAL) independently struggled on\n# the same class — Low pain F1 never exceeded ~0.32, and in 09C\n# collapsed to ~0.00-0.14. Two very different loss designs failing\n# on the same boundary suggests the label boundary itself may be\n# close to the limit of what a single still frame can show, not a\n# loss-function problem. This cell pulls the actual misclassified\n# frames from Stage 09B's validation predictions so you can look\n# at them yourself before investing more training time.\n#\n# Requires: models/stage09b/best_resnet18_stage09b.pth to exist\n# (from the Stage 09B cell). Does not modify the Stage 05B split,\n# does not touch the test set, does not retrain anything.\n# ================================================================\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom torchvision import transforms, models\n\nBASE = Path(\"/kaggle/working/capstone\")\nDATA = BASE / \"metadata\" / \"stage07\"\nCKPT_PATH = BASE / \"models\" / \"stage09b\" / \"best_resnet18_stage09b.pth\"\nFIG_OUT = BASE / \"figures\" / \"stage09_diagnostic\"\nFIG_OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"CAPSTONE — STAGE 09 DIAGNOSTIC\")\nprint(\"Visual audit of No-pain <-> Low-pain confusion\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nIMG_SIZE = 224\nNUM_CLASSES = 4\nlabels_map = {0: \"No pain\", 1: \"Low pain\", 2: \"Moderate pain\", 3: \"High pain\"}\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nprint(f\"\\nDevice: {device}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Load validation manifest (Stage 07 — unchanged)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nval = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"validation_model.csv\")\nprint(f\"Validation frames: {len(val):,}\")\n\nval_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n])\n\n\nclass PainDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, df, transform):\n        self.df = df.reset_index(drop=True)\n        self.transform = transform\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.df)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        r = self.df.iloc[i]\n        img = Image.open(r.image_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n        return self.transform(img), int(r.pain_class), i  # keep row index\n\n\nval_ds = PainDataset(val, val_tf)\nval_loader = DataLoader(val_ds, batch_size=64, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Rebuild Stage 09B's model architecture and load its checkpoint\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nassert CKPT_PATH.exists(), (\n    f\"Checkpoint not found at {CKPT_PATH}. Run the Stage 09B training \"\n    \"cell first — this diagnostic reuses its saved weights.\"\n)\n\nmodel = models.resnet18(weights=None)\nin_features = model.fc.in_features\nmodel.fc = nn.Sequential(\n    nn.Dropout(p=0.4),\n    nn.Linear(in_features, NUM_CLASSES),\n)\nckpt = torch.load(CKPT_PATH, map_location=device)\nmodel.load_state_dict(ckpt[\"model_state_dict\"])\nmodel = model.to(device).eval()\n\nprint(f\"\\nLoaded checkpoint from epoch {ckpt['epoch']} \"\n      f\"(val_macro_f1={ckpt['best_val_macro_f1']:.4f})\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Run inference over the full validation set once\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nall_true, all_pred, all_idx = [], [], []\n\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for images, lbls, idxs in val_loader:\n        images = images.to(device)\n        logits = model(images)\n        preds = logits.argmax(1).cpu().numpy()\n        all_true.extend(lbls.numpy())\n        all_pred.extend(preds)\n        all_idx.extend(idxs.numpy())\n\nval_results = val.iloc[all_idx].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\nval_results[\"true_class\"] = all_true\nval_results[\"pred_class\"] = all_pred\nval_results[\"true_label\"] = val_results.true_class.map(labels_map)\nval_results[\"pred_label\"] = val_results.pred_class.map(labels_map)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Isolate the specific confusion: true=No(0) & true=Low(1),\n# in both directions of error\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nlow_true_pred_no = val_results[\n    (val_results.true_class == 1) & (val_results.pred_class == 0)\n]\nno_true_pred_low = val_results[\n    (val_results.true_class == 0) & (val_results.pred_class == 1)\n]\nlow_correct = val_results[\n    (val_results.true_class == 1) & (val_results.pred_class == 1)\n]\n\nprint(\"\\nNo-pain <-> Low-pain confusion counts:\")\nprint(f\"  True Low, predicted No   (missed low pain)  : {len(low_true_pred_no):,}\")\nprint(f\"  True No,  predicted Low  (false alarm)       : {len(no_true_pred_low):,}\")\nprint(f\"  True Low, predicted Low  (correct)           : {len(low_correct):,}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Build a grid: rows = {misclassified Low->No, correct Low, misclassified No->Low}\n# Sample up to 10 per row for visual inspection\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nN_PER_ROW = 10\nSEED = 42\nrng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n\n\ndef sample_rows(df, n):\n    if len(df) == 0:\n        return df\n    n = min(n, len(df))\n    return df.iloc[rng.choice(len(df), size=n, replace=False)]\n\n\nrows_to_plot = [\n    (\"Missed Low pain\\n(true=Low, pred=No)\", sample_rows(low_true_pred_no, N_PER_ROW)),\n    (\"Correct Low pain\\n(true=Low, pred=Low)\", sample_rows(low_correct, N_PER_ROW)),\n    (\"False alarm\\n(true=No, pred=Low)\", sample_rows(no_true_pred_low, N_PER_ROW)),\n]\n\nn_rows = len(rows_to_plot)\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(n_rows, N_PER_ROW, figsize=(N_PER_ROW * 1.8, n_rows * 2.2))\n\nfor row_i, (row_title, sample_df) in enumerate(rows_to_plot):\n    for col_i in range(N_PER_ROW):\n        ax = axes[row_i, col_i] if n_rows > 1 else axes[col_i]\n        ax.axis(\"off\")\n        if col_i < len(sample_df):\n            r = sample_df.iloc[col_i]\n            try:\n                img = Image.open(r.image_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n                ax.imshow(img)\n                ax.set_title(f\"PSPI={int(r.pspi)}\", fontsize=8)\n            except Exception as e:\n                ax.text(0.5, 0.5, \"load\\nerror\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=7)\n        if col_i == 0:\n            ax.text(\n                -0.35, 0.5, row_title, transform=ax.transAxes,\n                fontsize=9, va=\"center\", ha=\"right\", rotation=0,\n            )\n\nplt.suptitle(\n    \"Stage 09B — No-pain vs Low-pain: misclassified and correct examples\\n\"\n    \"(PSPI label shown per frame; No=0, Low=1-3)\",\n    fontsize=11,\n)\nplt.tight_layout()\nfig_path = FIG_OUT / \"no_vs_low_pain_confusion_grid.png\"\nplt.savefig(fig_path, dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\nplt.show()\nplt.close()\n\nprint(f\"\\nSaved grid to: {fig_path}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Numeric check: PSPI distribution within each confusion bucket\n# If \"missed low pain\" frames cluster right at PSPI=1 (the lowest\n# possible non-zero score) while correct Low-pain frames skew\n# toward PSPI=3, that's strong evidence the boundary problem is a\n# labeling/severity issue, not a model issue — PSPI=1 frames may\n# be genuinely indistinguishable from PSPI=0 in a single still frame.\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nprint(\"\\nPSPI distribution within each bucket:\")\nfor name, df in [\n    (\"Missed Low pain (true=Low, pred=No)\", low_true_pred_no),\n    (\"Correct Low pain (true=Low, pred=Low)\", low_correct),\n    (\"False alarm (true=No, pred=Low)\", no_true_pred_low),\n]:\n    if len(df) > 0:\n        print(f\"\\n  {name}  (n={len(df)}):\")\n        print(f\"    {df.pspi.value_counts().sort_index().to_dict()}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"\\n  {name}  (n=0)\")\n\npct_missed_at_pspi1 = (\n    (low_true_pred_no.pspi == 1).mean() * 100 if len(low_true_pred_no) > 0 else float(\"nan\")\n)\npct_correct_at_pspi1 = (\n    (low_correct.pspi == 1).mean() * 100 if len(low_correct) > 0 else float(\"nan\")\n)\n\nprint(f\"\\n% of 'missed Low pain' frames at PSPI=1 (weakest possible signal): \"\n      f\"{pct_missed_at_pspi1:.1f}%\")\nprint(f\"% of 'correct Low pain' frames at PSPI=1: {pct_correct_at_pspi1:.1f}%\")\n\nif not np.isnan(pct_missed_at_pspi1) and not np.isnan(pct_correct_at_pspi1):\n    if pct_missed_at_pspi1 > pct_correct_at_pspi1 + 15:\n        print(\n            \"\\n-> Missed frames skew noticeably toward PSPI=1 relative to correct \"\n            \"ones. This supports treating PSPI=1 as a boundary-ambiguity case \"\n            \"rather than purely a model failure — consider merging No+Low into \"\n            \"a single 'minimal pain' class for a supplementary 3-class metric, \"\n            \"or noting this explicitly as a limitation in your writeup.\"\n        )\n    else:\n        print(\n            \"\\n-> No strong PSPI skew between missed and correct Low-pain frames. \"\n            \"The confusion doesn't look purely like a boundary-severity artifact — \"\n            \"worth also checking head pose/occlusion/lighting in the image grid \"\n            \"above for a possible visual (not just severity) explanation.\"\n        )\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Save the full confusion subset to CSV for further manual review\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nreview_cols = [\n    \"frame_id\", \"subject_group\", \"sequence_id\", \"frame_number\",\n    \"image_path\", \"pspi\", \"true_label\", \"pred_label\",\n]\nval_results[\n    (val_results.true_class.isin([0, 1])) & (val_results.pred_class.isin([0, 1]))\n][review_cols].to_csv(FIG_OUT / \"no_vs_low_pain_review.csv\", index=False)\n\nprint(f\"\\nFull No/Low review table saved to: \"\n      f\"{FIG_OUT / 'no_vs_low_pain_review.csv'}\")\nprint(\"\\nDone. Review the image grid above before deciding on next steps.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-04T16:04:55.451159Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-04T16:04:55.451494Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-04T16:05:32.949489Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-04T16:04:55.45146Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-04T16:05:32.948414Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"=================================================================\nCAPSTONE — STAGE 09 DIAGNOSTIC\nVisual audit of No-pain <-> Low-pain confusion\n=================================================================\n\nDevice: cuda\nValidation frames: 7,246\n\nLoaded checkpoint from epoch 21 (val_macro_f1=0.5944)\n\nNo-pain <-> Low-pain confusion counts:\n  True Low, predicted No   (missed low pain)  : 879\n  True No,  predicted Low  (false alarm)       : 514\n  True Low, predicted Low  (correct)           : 86\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1800x660 with 30 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"\nSaved grid to: /kaggle/working/capstone/figures/stage09_diagnostic/no_vs_low_pain_confusion_grid.png\n\nPSPI distribution within each bucket:\n\n  Missed Low pain (true=Low, pred=No)  (n=879):\n    {1.0: 446, 2.0: 335, 3.0: 98}\n\n  Correct Low pain (true=Low, pred=Low)  (n=86):\n    {1.0: 12, 2.0: 25, 3.0: 49}\n\n  False alarm (true=No, pred=Low)  (n=514):\n    {0.0: 514}\n\n% of 'missed Low pain' frames at PSPI=1 (weakest possible signal): 50.7%\n% of 'correct Low pain' frames at PSPI=1: 14.0%\n\n-> Missed frames skew noticeably toward PSPI=1 relative to correct ones. This supports treating PSPI=1 as a boundary-ambiguity case rather than purely a model failure — consider merging No+Low into a single 'minimal pain' class for a supplementary 3-class metric, or noting this explicitly as a limitation in your writeup.\n\nFull No/Low review table saved to: /kaggle/working/capstone/figures/stage09_diagnostic/no_vs_low_pain_review.csv\n\nDone. Review the image grid above before deciding on next steps.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ================================================================\n# CAPSTONE — STAGE 09-SUPPLEMENTARY METRICS\n# 1. 3-class macro-F1 (No+Low merged into \"Minimal/No pain\")\n#    — quantifies how much the PSPI=1 boundary issue is costing\n#      the headline 4-class number\n# 2. Per-PSPI-value accuracy table (0-15, not just the 4 bins)\n#    — shows the monotonic detectability gradient directly\n#\n# Reuses Stage 09B's saved checkpoint and predictions logic from\n# the diagnostic cell. Does not retrain anything, does not touch\n# the test set, does not modify the Stage 05B split.\n# ================================================================\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom torchvision import transforms, models\nfrom sklearn.metrics import f1_score, accuracy_score, balanced_accuracy_score, confusion_matrix\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nBASE = Path(\"/kaggle/working/capstone\")\nDATA = BASE / \"metadata\" / \"stage07\"\nCKPT_PATH = BASE / \"models\" / \"stage09b\" / \"best_resnet18_stage09b.pth\"\nOUT = BASE / \"models\" / \"stage09b\" / \"supplementary\"\nOUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"CAPSTONE — STAGE 09 SUPPLEMENTARY METRICS\")\nprint(\"3-class merged F1 + per-PSPI-value accuracy\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nIMG_SIZE = 224\nNUM_CLASSES = 4\nlabels_map = {0: \"No pain\", 1: \"Low pain\", 2: \"Moderate pain\", 3: \"High pain\"}\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nprint(f\"\\nDevice: {device}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Load validation manifest (Stage 07 — unchanged)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nval = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"validation_model.csv\")\nprint(f\"Validation frames: {len(val):,}\")\n\nval_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n])\n\n\nclass PainDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, df, transform):\n        self.df = df.reset_index(drop=True)\n        self.transform = transform\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.df)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        r = self.df.iloc[i]\n        img = Image.open(r.image_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n        return self.transform(img), int(r.pain_class), i\n\n\nval_ds = PainDataset(val, val_tf)\nval_loader = DataLoader(val_ds, batch_size=64, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Rebuild Stage 09B's model and load its checkpoint\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nassert CKPT_PATH.exists(), (\n    f\"Checkpoint not found at {CKPT_PATH}. Run the Stage 09B training \"\n    \"cell first.\"\n)\n\nmodel = models.resnet18(weights=None)\nin_features = model.fc.in_features\nmodel.fc = nn.Sequential(\n    nn.Dropout(p=0.4),\n    nn.Linear(in_features, NUM_CLASSES),\n)\nckpt = torch.load(CKPT_PATH, map_location=device)\nmodel.load_state_dict(ckpt[\"model_state_dict\"])\nmodel = model.to(device).eval()\n\nprint(f\"\\nLoaded checkpoint from epoch {ckpt['epoch']} \"\n      f\"(val_macro_f1={ckpt['best_val_macro_f1']:.4f})\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Run inference over the full validation set once\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nall_true, all_pred, all_idx = [], [], []\n\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for images, lbls, idxs in val_loader:\n        images = images.to(device)\n        logits = model(images)\n        preds = logits.argmax(1).cpu().numpy()\n        all_true.extend(lbls.numpy())\n        all_pred.extend(preds)\n        all_idx.extend(idxs.numpy())\n\nval_results = val.iloc[all_idx].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\nval_results[\"true_class\"] = all_true\nval_results[\"pred_class\"] = all_pred\n\n# ================================================================\n# PART 1 — 3-class supplementary metric (No + Low merged)\n# ================================================================\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"PART 1: 3-CLASS METRIC (No pain + Low pain merged)\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\n# Merge classes 0 and 1 -> single \"Minimal/No pain\" class 0.\n# Shift Moderate(2)->1, High(3)->2 so labels stay contiguous.\ndef merge_to_3class(x):\n    if x in (0, 1):\n        return 0\n    if x == 2:\n        return 1\n    return 2  # x == 3\n\n\ntrue_3c = val_results.true_class.apply(merge_to_3class).values\npred_3c = val_results.pred_class.apply(merge_to_3class).values\n\nlabels_3c = {0: \"Minimal/No pain\", 1: \"Moderate pain\", 2: \"High pain\"}\n\nacc_3c = accuracy_score(true_3c, pred_3c)\nbal_acc_3c = balanced_accuracy_score(true_3c, pred_3c)\nf1_3c = f1_score(true_3c, pred_3c, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\nf1_per_class_3c = f1_score(true_3c, pred_3c, average=None, zero_division=0, labels=[0, 1, 2])\ncm_3c = confusion_matrix(true_3c, pred_3c, labels=[0, 1, 2])\n\n# For comparison, the original 4-class metrics on this same checkpoint\nf1_4c = f1_score(val_results.true_class, val_results.pred_class, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\nacc_4c = accuracy_score(val_results.true_class, val_results.pred_class)\nbal_acc_4c = balanced_accuracy_score(val_results.true_class, val_results.pred_class)\n\nprint(f\"\\n4-class (original)  : Macro-F1={f1_4c:.4f} | Acc={acc_4c:.4f} | Bal Acc={bal_acc_4c:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"3-class (No+Low merged): Macro-F1={f1_3c:.4f} | Acc={acc_3c:.4f} | Bal Acc={bal_acc_3c:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"\\nMacro-F1 change from merging: {f1_3c - f1_4c:+.4f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nPer-class F1 (3-class):\")\nfor i, name in labels_3c.items():\n    print(f\"  {name:18s}: {f1_per_class_3c[i]:.4f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nConfusion matrix (3-class, rows=true, cols=pred):\")\nprint(f\"           {'  '.join(f'{labels_3c[i]:>16s}' for i in range(3))}\")\nfor i in range(3):\n    print(f\"  {labels_3c[i]:16s} {cm_3c[i]}\")\n\n# ================================================================\n# PART 2 — Per-PSPI-value accuracy table (raw scale, not bins)\n# ================================================================\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"PART 2: PER-PSPI-VALUE ACCURACY (4-class prediction)\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\n# For each exact PSPI value present in validation, compute:\n#  - how many frames have that PSPI value\n#  - which pain_class bin it falls into (ground truth)\n#  - accuracy of the model at recovering that bin for this PSPI value\n#  - most common predicted class for this PSPI value\nrows = []\nfor pspi_val in sorted(val_results.pspi.dropna().unique()):\n    subset = val_results[val_results.pspi == pspi_val]\n    if len(subset) == 0:\n        continue\n    true_bin = subset.true_class.iloc[0]  # constant within a pspi value\n    acc = (subset.pred_class == subset.true_class).mean()\n    pred_dist = subset.pred_class.value_counts(normalize=True).round(3).to_dict()\n    pred_dist_named = {labels_map[k]: v for k, v in sorted(pred_dist.items())}\n    rows.append({\n        \"pspi_value\": pspi_val,\n        \"true_bin\": labels_map[true_bin],\n        \"n_frames\": len(subset),\n        \"accuracy\": round(acc, 4),\n        \"prediction_distribution\": pred_dist_named,\n    })\n\npspi_table = pd.DataFrame(rows)\npd.set_option(\"display.max_colwidth\", None)\nprint(\"\\n\" + pspi_table.to_string(index=False))\n\npspi_table.to_csv(OUT / \"per_pspi_value_accuracy.csv\", index=False)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Highlight the gradient within the Low-pain bin specifically,\n# since that's the bin driving the headline F1 ceiling\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nlow_bin_table = pspi_table[pspi_table.true_bin == \"Low pain\"]\nprint(\"\\n--- Detectability gradient within the Low-pain bin (PSPI 1-3) ---\")\nprint(low_bin_table[[\"pspi_value\", \"n_frames\", \"accuracy\"]].to_string(index=False))\n\nif len(low_bin_table) >= 2:\n    acc_low = low_bin_table.sort_values(\"pspi_value\").accuracy.values\n    if acc_low[0] < acc_low[-1]:\n        print(\n            f\"\\n-> Accuracy rises monotonically from PSPI={int(low_bin_table.pspi_value.min())} \"\n            f\"({acc_low[0]:.1%}) to PSPI={int(low_bin_table.pspi_value.max())} ({acc_low[-1]:.1%}) \"\n            \"within the Low-pain bin, confirming detectability scales with severity \"\n            \"even inside a single class bin.\"\n        )\n\n# ================================================================\n# Save combined summary JSON\n# ================================================================\nsummary = {\n    \"source_checkpoint\": str(CKPT_PATH),\n    \"source_epoch\": ckpt[\"epoch\"],\n    \"metrics_4class\": {\n        \"macro_f1\": float(f1_4c),\n        \"accuracy\": float(acc_4c),\n        \"balanced_accuracy\": float(bal_acc_4c),\n    },\n    \"metrics_3class_no_low_merged\": {\n        \"macro_f1\": float(f1_3c),\n        \"accuracy\": float(acc_3c),\n        \"balanced_accuracy\": float(bal_acc_3c),\n        \"per_class_f1\": {labels_3c[i]: float(f1_per_class_3c[i]) for i in range(3)},\n        \"confusion_matrix\": cm_3c.tolist(),\n        \"class_order\": [labels_3c[i] for i in range(3)],\n    },\n    \"macro_f1_gain_from_merging_no_and_low\": float(f1_3c - f1_4c),\n    \"per_pspi_value_accuracy_file\": str(OUT / \"per_pspi_value_accuracy.csv\"),\n    \"note\": (\n        \"3-class metric merges 'No pain' (PSPI=0) and 'Low pain' (PSPI 1-3) \"\n        \"into a single 'Minimal/No pain' class, since diagnostic analysis \"\n        \"showed PSPI=1 frames are detected far less reliably (50.7% of \"\n        \"misses were at PSPI=1) than PSPI=2-3 frames within the same bin. \"\n        \"Reported as a supplementary metric alongside the primary 4-class \"\n        \"result, not a replacement for it.\"\n    ),\n}\n\nwith open(OUT / \"supplementary_metrics_summary.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"SUPPLEMENTARY METRICS COMPLETED\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(f\"3-class table + summary saved to: {OUT}\")\nprint(f\"  - per_pspi_value_accuracy.csv\")\nprint(f\"  - supplementary_metrics_summary.json\")\nprint(f\"\\n4-class Macro-F1: {f1_4c:.4f}  ->  3-class Macro-F1: {f1_3c:.4f} \"\n      f\"({f1_3c - f1_4c:+.4f})\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-04T16:26:12.837526Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-04T16:26:12.838355Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-04T16:26:47.899204Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-04T16:26:12.838316Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-04T16:26:47.898091Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"=================================================================\nCAPSTONE — STAGE 09 SUPPLEMENTARY METRICS\n3-class merged F1 + per-PSPI-value accuracy\n=================================================================\n\nDevice: cuda\nValidation frames: 7,246\n\nLoaded checkpoint from epoch 21 (val_macro_f1=0.5944)\n\n=================================================================\nPART 1: 3-CLASS METRIC (No pain + Low pain merged)\n=================================================================\n\n4-class (original)  : Macro-F1=0.5944 | Acc=0.7843 | Bal Acc=0.5659\n3-class (No+Low merged): Macro-F1=0.7937 | Acc=0.9765 | Bal Acc=0.7535\n\nMacro-F1 change from merging: +0.1993\n\nPer-class F1 (3-class):\n  Minimal/No pain   : 0.9878\n  Moderate pain     : 0.6620\n  High pain         : 0.7312\n\nConfusion matrix (3-class, rows=true, cols=pred):\n            Minimal/No pain     Moderate pain         High pain\n  Minimal/No pain  [6900   83    0]\n  Moderate pain    [ 62 142   0]\n  High pain        [25  0 34]\n\n=================================================================\nPART 2: PER-PSPI-VALUE ACCURACY (4-class prediction)\n=================================================================\n\n pspi_value      true_bin  n_frames  accuracy                                       prediction_distribution\n        0.0       No pain      5998    0.9038 {'No pain': 0.904, 'Low pain': 0.086, 'Moderate pain': 0.011}\n        1.0      Low pain       458    0.0262                         {'No pain': 0.974, 'Low pain': 0.026}\n        2.0      Low pain       362    0.0691 {'No pain': 0.925, 'Low pain': 0.069, 'Moderate pain': 0.006}\n        3.0      Low pain       165    0.2970 {'No pain': 0.594, 'Low pain': 0.297, 'Moderate pain': 0.109}\n        4.0 Moderate pain       102    0.7059 {'No pain': 0.167, 'Low pain': 0.127, 'Moderate pain': 0.706}\n        5.0 Moderate pain        30    0.8000                        {'No pain': 0.2, 'Moderate pain': 0.8}\n        6.0 Moderate pain        72    0.6389 {'No pain': 0.028, 'Low pain': 0.333, 'Moderate pain': 0.639}\n       10.0     High pain        49    0.5918                       {'Low pain': 0.408, 'High pain': 0.592}\n       12.0     High pain        10    0.5000                           {'Low pain': 0.5, 'High pain': 0.5}\n\n--- Detectability gradient within the Low-pain bin (PSPI 1-3) ---\n pspi_value  n_frames  accuracy\n        1.0       458    0.0262\n        2.0       362    0.0691\n        3.0       165    0.2970\n\n-> Accuracy rises monotonically from PSPI=1 (2.6%) to PSPI=3 (29.7%) within the Low-pain bin, confirming detectability scales with severity even inside a single class bin.\n\n=================================================================\nSUPPLEMENTARY METRICS COMPLETED\n=================================================================\n3-class table + summary saved to: /kaggle/working/capstone/models/stage09b/supplementary\n  - per_pspi_value_accuracy.csv\n  - supplementary_metrics_summary.json\n\n4-class Macro-F1: 0.5944  ->  3-class Macro-F1: 0.7937 (+0.1993)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Motivation (from Stage 09 diagnostics):\n  Stage 09B (per-frame ResNet18 + Focal Loss) hit macro-F1=0.594,\n  and root-cause analysis showed the ceiling is concentrated at\n  PSPI=1: only 2.6% of PSPI=1 frames are correctly classified,\n  rising monotonically to 6.9% at PSPI=2 and 29.7% at PSPI=3.\n  Three different loss functions (CE, Focal, CORAL) all hit the\n  same wall, which means the problem is that a single still frame\n  at PSPI=1 does not contain enough signal — not that the loss\n  function is wrong. Pain onset is a temporal phenomenon (an AU\n  activating over several frames); a lone frame at the faintest\n  point of that activation looks close to neutral.\n\nThis stage fixes that by classifying a WINDOW of consecutive\nframes from the same sequence instead of a single frame:\n  ResNet18 (frame-level feature extractor, warm-started from the\n  Stage 09B checkpoint) -> per-frame feature vectors -> GRU over\n  the window -> classify the window's center frame.\n\nUses the same Stage 05B locked split and Stage 07 pain_class\nbins. Does not modify the split. Does not touch the test set.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ================================================================\n# CAPSTONE — STAGE 10 | TEMPORAL SEQUENCE MODEL (CNN + GRU)\n# ================================================================\nimport json, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader, WeightedRandomSampler\nfrom torchvision import transforms, models\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (\n    accuracy_score,\n    balanced_accuracy_score,\n    f1_score,\n    confusion_matrix,\n)\n\nBASE = Path(\"/kaggle/working/capstone\")\nDATA = BASE / \"metadata\" / \"stage07\"\nSTAGE09B_CKPT = BASE / \"models\" / \"stage09b\" / \"best_resnet18_stage09b.pth\"\nOUT = BASE / \"models\" / \"stage10\"\nOUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"CAPSTONE — STAGE 10\")\nprint(\"Temporal Sequence Model (CNN + GRU over frame windows)\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Configuration\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nSEED = 42\nIMG_SIZE = 224\nWINDOW_SIZE = 7             # odd number: 3 frames before/after center\nWINDOW_HALF = WINDOW_SIZE // 2\nBATCH_SIZE = 16             # smaller than Stage 09 since each item is a full window\nNUM_WORKERS = 2\nMAX_EPOCHS = 30\nLR = 3e-5\nGRU_HIDDEN = 128\nGRU_LAYERS = 1\nWEIGHT_DECAY = 1e-4\nNUM_CLASSES = 4\nDROPOUT_P = 0.4\nFOCAL_GAMMA = 2.0\nLABEL_SMOOTHING = 0.1\nEARLY_STOP_PATIENCE = 7\nPLATEAU_PATIENCE = 3\nPLATEAU_FACTOR = 0.5\n\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nprint(f\"\\nDevice : {device}\")\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    print(f\"GPU    : {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")\n\nlabels_map = {0: \"No pain\", 1: \"Low pain\", 2: \"Moderate pain\", 3: \"High pain\"}\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Load Stage 07 manifests (locked Stage 05B split — UNCHANGED)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ntrain = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"train_model.csv\")\nval = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"validation_model.csv\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nTrain frames      : {len(train):,}\")\nprint(f\"Validation frames : {len(val):,}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Build ordered per-sequence frame lookups, so a window never\n# crosses a sequence boundary or a split boundary. Each usable\n# center frame must have WINDOW_HALF neighbors on both sides\n# within the SAME sequence_id.\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ndef build_window_index(df):\n    \"\"\"Returns a list of dicts: each is one training/eval example,\n    containing the center row's label and the ordered list of\n    WINDOW_SIZE image paths (padded by edge-repeating when a\n    sequence is shorter than the window, which only happens at\n    the very start/end of a sequence).\"\"\"\n    df = df.sort_values([\"sequence_id\", \"frame_number\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n    windows = []\n    for seq_id, group in df.groupby(\"sequence_id\"):\n        group = group.reset_index(drop=True)\n        paths = group.image_path.tolist()\n        labels = group.pain_class.tolist()\n        frame_ids = group.frame_id.tolist()\n        n = len(group)\n        for center_i in range(n):\n            idxs = []\n            for offset in range(-WINDOW_HALF, WINDOW_HALF + 1):\n                j = center_i + offset\n                j = max(0, min(n - 1, j))  # edge-repeat padding\n                idxs.append(j)\n            windows.append({\n                \"sequence_id\": seq_id,\n                \"center_frame_id\": frame_ids[center_i],\n                \"label\": int(labels[center_i]),\n                \"image_paths\": [paths[j] for j in idxs],\n            })\n    return windows\n\n\nprint(\"\\nBuilding frame windows (this walks every sequence once)...\")\ntrain_windows = build_window_index(train)\nval_windows = build_window_index(val)\nprint(f\"Train windows      : {len(train_windows):,}\")\nprint(f\"Validation windows : {len(val_windows):,}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Transforms — same normalization as Stage 09; lighter augmentation\n# since temporal jitter from the window itself already adds variety\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ntrain_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5),\n    transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.15, contrast=0.15),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n])\n\nval_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n])\n\n\nclass PainWindowDataset(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"Each item is a (WINDOW_SIZE, C, H, W) tensor of consecutive\n    frames from one sequence, plus the center frame's label. The\n    SAME random flip/jitter is applied to every frame in a window\n    (not independently per-frame), so temporal consistency within\n    the window is preserved under augmentation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, windows, transform, apply_flip_consistently=False):\n        self.windows = windows\n        self.transform = transform\n        self.apply_flip_consistently = apply_flip_consistently\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.windows)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        w = self.windows[i]\n        do_flip = self.apply_flip_consistently and (np.random.rand() < 0.5)\n\n        frames = []\n        for path in w[\"image_paths\"]:\n            img = Image.open(path).convert(\"RGB\")\n            if do_flip:\n                img = transforms.functional.hflip(img)\n            # apply the rest of the transform pipeline minus the\n            # random-flip step (already handled above) to keep the\n            # flip consistent across the whole window\n            img = transforms.functional.resize(img, (IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE))\n            img = transforms.functional.to_tensor(img)\n            img = transforms.functional.normalize(\n                img, [0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]\n            )\n            frames.append(img)\n\n        clip = torch.stack(frames, dim=0)  # (T, C, H, W)\n        y = torch.tensor(w[\"label\"], dtype=torch.long)\n        return clip, y\n\n\ntrain_ds = PainWindowDataset(train_windows, train_tf, apply_flip_consistently=True)\nval_ds = PainWindowDataset(val_windows, val_tf, apply_flip_consistently=False)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# WeightedRandomSampler — same rationale as Stage 09B, computed\n# over window centers (severe imbalance persists at window level\n# since it's inherited from the frame-level pain_class)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ntrain_center_labels = np.array([w[\"label\"] for w in train_windows])\nclass_counts = pd.Series(train_center_labels).value_counts().sort_index()\nclass_sample_weights = {int(k): 1.0 / v for k, v in class_counts.items()}\nsample_weights = np.array([class_sample_weights[l] for l in train_center_labels])\nsampler = WeightedRandomSampler(\n    weights=sample_weights, num_samples=len(sample_weights), replacement=True,\n)\n\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(\n    train_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, sampler=sampler,\n    num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True,\n)\nval_loader = DataLoader(\n    val_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False,\n    num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True,\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSampler class weights (1/frequency, computed on window centers):\")\nfor k, v in class_sample_weights.items():\n    print(f\"  {labels_map[k]:15s}: {v:.6f}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Model — ResNet18 feature extractor (warm-started from Stage 09B)\n# + GRU over the window + classifier on the final hidden state\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nclass CNNGRUPainModel(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, num_classes, gru_hidden=128, gru_layers=1, dropout_p=0.4):\n        super().__init__()\n        backbone = models.resnet18(weights=models.ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT)\n        feat_dim = backbone.fc.in_features\n        backbone.fc = nn.Identity()\n        self.backbone = backbone\n        self.feat_dim = feat_dim\n\n        self.gru = nn.GRU(\n            input_size=feat_dim,\n            hidden_size=gru_hidden,\n            num_layers=gru_layers,\n            batch_first=True,\n            bidirectional=True,\n        )\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(p=dropout_p)\n        self.classifier = nn.Linear(gru_hidden * 2, num_classes)  # *2 for bidirectional\n\n    def forward(self, clips):\n        # clips: (B, T, C, H, W)\n        B, T, C, H, W = clips.shape\n        flat = clips.view(B * T, C, H, W)\n        feats = self.backbone(flat)                 # (B*T, feat_dim)\n        feats = feats.view(B, T, self.feat_dim)      # (B, T, feat_dim)\n\n        gru_out, _ = self.gru(feats)                 # (B, T, 2*hidden)\n        center_idx = T // 2\n        center_repr = gru_out[:, center_idx, :]      # representation at the center frame\n        center_repr = self.dropout(center_repr)\n        logits = self.classifier(center_repr)\n        return logits\n\n\nmodel = CNNGRUPainModel(\n    num_classes=NUM_CLASSES, gru_hidden=GRU_HIDDEN,\n    gru_layers=GRU_LAYERS, dropout_p=DROPOUT_P,\n).to(device)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Warm-start the CNN backbone from Stage 09B's fine-tuned weights\n# rather than plain ImageNet init — it already learned pain-relevant\n# per-frame features, the GRU just needs to add temporal context\n# on top of that.\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nif STAGE09B_CKPT.exists():\n    print(f\"\\nWarm-starting backbone from Stage 09B checkpoint: {STAGE09B_CKPT}\")\n    ckpt09b = torch.load(STAGE09B_CKPT, map_location=device)\n    state09b = ckpt09b[\"model_state_dict\"]\n    # Stage 09B's state dict has backbone.* keys plus its own fc.*\n    # (Dropout+Linear) head, which we don't reuse here. Filter to\n    # only load matching backbone weights.\n    backbone_state = {\n        k: v for k, v in state09b.items()\n        if not k.startswith(\"fc.\")\n    }\n    missing, unexpected = model.backbone.load_state_dict(backbone_state, strict=False)\n    print(f\"  Loaded backbone weights. Missing keys: {len(missing)}, \"\n          f\"unexpected: {len(unexpected)}\")\nelse:\n    print(f\"\\nWARNING: Stage 09B checkpoint not found at {STAGE09B_CKPT}. \"\n          f\"Falling back to plain ImageNet-pretrained backbone.\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Focal loss (best-performing loss from Stage 09B; CORAL was\n# tried in Stage 09C and underperformed — see Stage 09 findings)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\ncounts = pd.Series(train_center_labels).value_counts().sort_index()\nalpha = torch.tensor(\n    [len(train_center_labels) / (NUM_CLASSES * counts.get(i, 0)) for i in range(NUM_CLASSES)],\n    dtype=torch.float32, device=device,\n)\nalpha = alpha / alpha.sum() * NUM_CLASSES\n\nprint(\"\\nFocal loss alpha (class weights):\")\nfor i, a in enumerate(alpha):\n    print(f\"  {labels_map[i]:15s}: {a.item():.4f}\")\n\n\nclass FocalLoss(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, alpha, gamma=2.0, label_smoothing=0.0):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.alpha = alpha\n        self.gamma = gamma\n        self.label_smoothing = label_smoothing\n\n    def forward(self, logits, targets):\n        ce = F.cross_entropy(\n            logits, targets, reduction=\"none\",\n            label_smoothing=self.label_smoothing,\n        )\n        pt = torch.exp(-ce)\n        at = self.alpha[targets]\n        loss = at * (1 - pt) ** self.gamma * ce\n        return loss.mean()\n\n\ncriterion = FocalLoss(alpha=alpha, gamma=FOCAL_GAMMA, label_smoothing=LABEL_SMOOTHING)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Optimizer / scheduler — same stabilized recipe validated in\n# Stage 09C (no frozen phase, ReduceLROnPlateau)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\noptimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=LR, weight_decay=WEIGHT_DECAY)\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(\n    optimizer, mode=\"max\", factor=PLATEAU_FACTOR, patience=PLATEAU_PATIENCE,\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Training loop\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nhistory = []\nval_f1_raw_history = []\nMOVING_AVG_WINDOW = 3\nbest_f1_smoothed = -1\nbest_epoch = -1\nepochs_without_improvement = 0\n\nfor epoch in range(1, MAX_EPOCHS + 1):\n    start = time.time()\n    model.train()\n\n    train_loss = 0\n    train_true, train_pred = [], []\n\n    for clips, lbls in train_loader:\n        clips = clips.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n        lbls = lbls.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n        logits = model(clips)\n        loss = criterion(logits, lbls)\n        loss.backward()\n        optimizer.step()\n\n        train_loss += loss.item() * clips.size(0)\n        train_true.extend(lbls.detach().cpu().numpy())\n        train_pred.extend(logits.argmax(1).detach().cpu().numpy())\n\n    train_loss /= len(train_ds)\n    train_acc = accuracy_score(train_true, train_pred)\n    train_f1 = f1_score(train_true, train_pred, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\n\n    # ---- Validation ----\n    model.eval()\n    val_loss = 0\n    val_true, val_pred = [], []\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for clips, lbls in val_loader:\n            clips = clips.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n            lbls = lbls.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n\n            logits = model(clips)\n            loss = criterion(logits, lbls)\n\n            val_loss += loss.item() * clips.size(0)\n            val_true.extend(lbls.cpu().numpy())\n            val_pred.extend(logits.argmax(1).cpu().numpy())\n\n    val_loss /= len(val_ds)\n    val_acc = accuracy_score(val_true, val_pred)\n    val_bal_acc = balanced_accuracy_score(val_true, val_pred)\n    val_f1 = f1_score(val_true, val_pred, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\n    val_f1_per_class = f1_score(\n        val_true, val_pred, average=None, zero_division=0, labels=list(range(NUM_CLASSES))\n    )\n    cm = confusion_matrix(val_true, val_pred, labels=list(range(NUM_CLASSES)))\n\n    val_f1_raw_history.append(val_f1)\n    val_f1_smoothed = float(np.mean(val_f1_raw_history[-MOVING_AVG_WINDOW:]))\n    scheduler.step(val_f1_smoothed)\n\n    elapsed = time.time() - start\n\n    row = {\n        \"epoch\": epoch,\n        \"train_loss\": train_loss,\n        \"train_accuracy\": train_acc,\n        \"train_macro_f1\": train_f1,\n        \"val_loss\": val_loss,\n        \"val_accuracy\": val_acc,\n        \"val_balanced_accuracy\": val_bal_acc,\n        \"val_macro_f1\": val_f1,\n        \"val_macro_f1_smoothed\": val_f1_smoothed,\n        \"lr\": optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"],\n        \"time_sec\": elapsed,\n    }\n    for i in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n        row[f\"val_f1_class_{i}_{labels_map[i].replace(' ', '_')}\"] = val_f1_per_class[i]\n    history.append(row)\n\n    print(\n        f\"Epoch {epoch:02d}/{MAX_EPOCHS} | \"\n        f\"Train Loss {train_loss:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Loss {val_loss:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Acc {val_acc:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Bal Acc {val_bal_acc:.4f} | \"\n        f\"Val Macro-F1 {val_f1:.4f} (smoothed {val_f1_smoothed:.4f}) | \"\n        f\"LR {optimizer.param_groups[0]['lr']:.2e} | \"\n        f\"{elapsed:.1f}s\"\n    )\n    print(f\"  Per-class F1: \" + \", \".join(\n        f\"{labels_map[i]}={val_f1_per_class[i]:.3f}\" for i in range(NUM_CLASSES)\n    ))\n    print(f\"  Confusion matrix (rows=true, cols=pred):\\n{cm}\")\n\n    if val_f1_smoothed > best_f1_smoothed:\n        best_f1_smoothed = val_f1_smoothed\n        best_epoch = epoch\n        epochs_without_improvement = 0\n\n        torch.save({\n            \"stage\": \"10\",\n            \"epoch\": epoch,\n            \"model_state_dict\": model.state_dict(),\n            \"optimizer_state_dict\": optimizer.state_dict(),\n            \"best_val_macro_f1_raw\": val_f1,\n            \"best_val_macro_f1_smoothed\": best_f1_smoothed,\n            \"window_size\": WINDOW_SIZE,\n            \"gru_hidden\": GRU_HIDDEN,\n            \"gru_layers\": GRU_LAYERS,\n            \"seed\": SEED,\n            \"img_size\": IMG_SIZE,\n            \"num_classes\": NUM_CLASSES,\n            \"confusion_matrix\": cm.tolist(),\n        }, OUT / \"best_cnn_gru_stage10.pth\")\n\n        print(f\"  ✓ Best checkpoint saved (smoothed Macro-F1={best_f1_smoothed:.4f}, \"\n              f\"raw={val_f1:.4f})\")\n    else:\n        epochs_without_improvement += 1\n        print(f\"  No improvement for {epochs_without_improvement} epoch(s) \"\n              f\"(best smoothed={best_f1_smoothed:.4f} @ epoch {best_epoch})\")\n\n    if epochs_without_improvement >= EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE:\n        print(f\"\\n>>> Early stopping triggered at epoch {epoch} \"\n              f\"(no improvement in {EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE} epochs)\")\n        break\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Save history + summary\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nhistory_df = pd.DataFrame(history)\nhistory_df.to_csv(OUT / \"training_history_stage10.csv\", index=False)\n\nbest_row = history_df.loc[history_df[\"epoch\"] == best_epoch].iloc[0]\n\nsummary = {\n    \"stage\": \"10\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"model\": f\"ResNet18 (warm-started from Stage 09B) + Bidirectional GRU \"\n             f\"(hidden={GRU_HIDDEN}, layers={GRU_LAYERS}) over {WINDOW_SIZE}-frame windows\",\n    \"window_size\": WINDOW_SIZE,\n    \"warm_start_checkpoint\": str(STAGE09B_CKPT),\n    \"image_size\": IMG_SIZE,\n    \"batch_size\": BATCH_SIZE,\n    \"max_epochs\": MAX_EPOCHS,\n    \"epochs_run\": len(history_df),\n    \"lr\": LR,\n    \"loss\": f\"FocalLoss(gamma={FOCAL_GAMMA}, label_smoothing={LABEL_SMOOTHING})\",\n    \"sampler\": \"WeightedRandomSampler (inverse class frequency, computed on window centers)\",\n    \"scheduler\": f\"ReduceLROnPlateau(factor={PLATEAU_FACTOR}, patience={PLATEAU_PATIENCE})\",\n    \"early_stop_patience\": EARLY_STOP_PATIENCE,\n    \"checkpoint_selection_metric\": f\"{MOVING_AVG_WINDOW}-epoch moving average of val_macro_f1\",\n    \"best_epoch\": int(best_epoch),\n    \"best_validation_macro_f1_smoothed\": float(best_f1_smoothed),\n    \"best_validation_macro_f1_raw\": float(best_row.val_macro_f1),\n    \"best_validation_accuracy\": float(best_row.val_accuracy),\n    \"best_validation_balanced_accuracy\": float(best_row.val_balanced_accuracy),\n    \"test_evaluation\": False,\n    \"stage05b_split_modified\": False,\n    \"comparison_to_prior_stages\": {\n        \"stage09_baseline_macro_f1\": 0.4666,\n        \"stage09b_focal_loss_macro_f1\": 0.5944,\n        \"stage09c_coral_macro_f1\": 0.5811,\n        \"stage10_temporal_macro_f1\": float(best_row.val_macro_f1),\n    },\n}\n\nwith open(OUT / \"stage10_summary.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"STAGE 10 COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(f\"Best checkpoint  : {OUT / 'best_cnn_gru_stage10.pth'}\")\nprint(f\"Training history : {OUT / 'training_history_stage10.csv'}\")\nprint(f\"Summary          : {OUT / 'stage10_summary.json'}\")\nprint(f\"Best Macro-F1    : smoothed={best_f1_smoothed:.4f}, raw={best_row.val_macro_f1:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"  (Stage 09 baseline: 0.4666 | Stage 09B: 0.5944 | Stage 09C CORAL: 0.5811)\")\nprint(f\"Best epoch       : {best_epoch}\")\nprint(\"Test set         : NOT USED\")\nprint(\"Stage 05B split  : UNCHANGED\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T08:49:35.177522Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T08:49:35.1799Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T10:50:38.938854Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-06T08:49:35.179858Z","shell.execute_reply